WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
A firework shell climbs into the
night sky on a long, curving path.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.060
Then it bursts.

3
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.980
Glowing pieces fly out in every direction,

4
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.830
each on its own path.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.430
Together, those pieces still have one
point where their total mass can be treated

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.840
as concentrated.

7
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.460
Ignore air resistance.

8
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.350
After the burst, what path
does that point follow?

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.520
In this mission, you'll draw
a boundary around a system,

10
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.780
and sort its forces into
internal and external.

11
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.760
Then you'll see when an object can
be treated as one simple object,

12
00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.880
and when its insides matter.

13
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.660
Your mission: predict the path
of that point after the burst,

14
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.250
and explain your prediction.
